{
  "requires": "reader-routing",
  "note": "Frames recorded with SCROLL_RECORD_SPECS=1 from ReaderView on the ScrollSim simulator and checked against Reference/reader-dark.png. They are XCUITest *accessibility* frames: for a text element that is the union of its glyph boxes and for a control it includes the tap padding, so it is not always the visual box. Elements whose box is content-driven (the page container, the verse block, the reference line) are asserted for existence only; the chrome, which is the layout this screen has to hold, is asserted by frame. The spec stays wrapped in a `spec` envelope so LayoutSpecTests' loader, which decodes every bare JSON in the bundle, leaves it to ReaderTests, which unwraps it. The translation pill is 62.2 pt wide, not the 72.0 recorded when its abbreviation read CLEAR: commit 82b8468 made the default translation's badge read ITANI. reader.hint is 209.2 (214 pt in the app's own space): ToastHint used to size itself to its text and came out at 262.7, and commit 70aaf51 pinned it to the 214 pt measured off the reference.",
  "spec": {
    "id": "reader-dark",
    "route": "reader",
    "appearance": "dark",
    "reference": { "width": 393, "height": 852 },
    "tolerance": 6,
    "elements": [
      { "name": "screen.reader", "query": "identifier", "frame": { "x": 0, "y": 0, "width": 393, "height": 852 }, "existenceOnly": true },
      { "name": "reader.pager", "query": "identifier", "frame": { "x": 0, "y": 0, "width": 393, "height": 852 }, "existenceOnly": true },
